data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":422,"output_index":1,"item":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_032d8c994a0816a5016adb365ecc348191b6e9b4368b1dffd3","call_id":"call_c0f0ae49db63478a875cc32a075a8126","name":"submit_artifact","arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"base_candidate\\\":1,\\\"patches\\\":[{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/text\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Using the basis proved in S001, define E_ab by E_ab(e_b)=e_a and E_ab(e_t)=0 for t!=b. The divided-power formulas give Y_lambda X_lambda=E_lambda,lambda: X_lambda kills e_i for i<lambda and sends e_lambda to e_0, while Y_lambda sends e_0 to e_lambda. For each fixed i with 0<=i<=lambda, put r=lambda-i. On the specific input e_lambda, S001's formula gives X_r e_lambda=binom(lambda-lambda+r,r)e_(lambda-r)=binom(r,r)e_i=e_i. Since E_lambda,lambda kills every e_t except e_lambda, X_(lambda-i)E_lambda,lambda=E_i,lambda. For each j with 0<=j<=lambda, put s=lambda-j. The formula gives Y_s e_j=binom(j+s,s)e_(j+s)=binom(lambda,lambda-j)e_lambda=binom(lambda,j)e_lambda. If t!=j, Y_s e_t is either zero or a multiple of e_(t+s), whose index is not lambda, so E_lambda,lambda Y_s e_t=0; hence E_lambda,lambda Y_(lambda-j)=binom(lambda,j)E_lambda,j. Since 0<=j<=lambda<p, neither lambda! nor j!(lambda-j)! is divisible by p, so binom(lambda,j) is a unit in R=Z_(p); this includes lambda=0 (the empty factorial is 1) and p=2. Therefore E_lambda,j=binom(lambda,j)^(-1)E_lambda,lambda Y_(lambda-j), and E_i,j=E_i,lambda E_lambda,j. Thus every matrix unit is in the R-algebra generated by the divided powers and preserves M_R.\\\"}]}\"}","status":"completed"}}

